      "body": "## Summary\n\nFix two Gemma4 tool-parser array cases: a quoted `]` inside a nested array must stay part of the string, and a stray closing bracket in a bare value must stop parsing instead of looping forever. The change follows the merged vLLM fix in https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/41991 and keeps the no-progress guard scoped to arrays.\n\nRegression coverage includes nested quoted brackets and a stray closing bracket. The branch is rebased onto current main.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Full `test_function_call_parser.py` module: **252 passed** on CPU with the branch's pinned `xgrammar==0.2.7`. The focused Gemma4 selector also passed all 19 tests.\n- All applicable changed-file pre-commit hooks and `git diff --check` pass.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Code formatting and style checks.\n- [x] Unit regression coverage.\n- [x] Documentation: No API change; parser behavior described above.\n- [x] Model accuracy and speed benchmarks are not applicable to this parsing/request-normalization fix.\n",
