  "issue_comments": [
    {
      "body": "Addressed the portability note: `_time_limit` now no-ops on platforms without `signal.SIGALRM` (i.e. non-POSIX), so the test still runs there—just without the hard timeout—while the assertions still catch a corrupted/non-terminating parse. Pushed.",
      "created_at": "2026-06-22T06:56:43Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/28857#issuecomment-4765684241",
      "id": 4765684241,
      "updated_at": "2026-06-22T06:56:43Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "EazyReal"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "@CatherineSue @JustinTong0323 @kpham-sgl @pyc96 could this get Gemma4 tool-parser review and the `run-ci` label?\n\nSmall parser-only fix: bracket characters inside quoted array strings no longer corrupt depth tracking, and a stray `]` can no longer spin the parse loop.",
      "created_at": "2026-06-25T03:14:48Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/28857#issuecomment-4795491438",
      "id": 4795491438,
